# Artifact Registry

Instead of creating standalone reports in arbitrary locations, **every generated artifact must be registered** in `artifact-registry.md`.

Prefer path: `docs/artifact-registry.md` when `docs/` exists; otherwise project root `artifact-registry.md`.

## Required entry fields

| Field | Content |
|-------|---------|
| **artifact** | Path to the generated file |
| **producer skill** | Skill that wrote it (e.g. `verify-todo`) |
| **generation date** | YYYY-MM-DD (ISO) |
| **purpose** | Why the artifact exists |
| **status** | `draft` / `final` / `superseded` / `failed` / `active` |
| **downstream consumers** | Skills, tasks, or humans that use it |

## Scope

Register every generated:

- report
- graph (including `.mmd`)
- manifest
- checkpoint
- sync summary, audit, Methods/Results drafts, figure plans, acquisition logs when produced as deliverables

Living files that skills update (`todo.md`, `method-decision.md`) must have a registry entry created on first write and **updated** (date + status) on subsequent material changes.

## Rules

- Append or update entries — do not delete history; mark old paths `superseded` when replaced
- Register immediately after writing the artifact
- Unregistered deliverables are incomplete work
- Consumers should discover artifacts via the registry when possible
